### About

**About section**

```text
You're winning more work than ever. The lads are flat out. But the final account lands and the number is forty grand short, and you can't fully explain why.

That's the one I keep hearing. And it's the one I spent fifteen years learning how to fix from the inside.

I started as a Project Engineer at Northern M&E, moved into contracts management, and finished as Operations Director at Harlow & Pike Building Services, where I grew the HVAC division from £4.2m to £11.8m in five years. We got there by fixing the same problems I see in most M&E and HVAC firms: margin bleeding out on jobs with no clear explanation, retentions sitting unpaid for months with nobody chasing them, and the MD still fielding every call they should never have to answer.

I now work with MDs and owners of M&E, HVAC and electrical contracting firms to get real visibility on where the money is going, get the retention cash moving, and get them out of the operational middle.

This is for you if:
- You're turning over £2m to £12m and the profit isn't following the revenue
- Final accounts keep landing short and you can't put your finger on why
- You're the first call for every site decision, including on the days you're supposed to be off
- You've got retentions sitting out there from jobs finished a year ago that nobody's chasing properly

I get into job reviews and pricing discussions from week one. There's no warm-up period. I already know what a retention looks like, how a variation gets absorbed, and what happens when an MC squeezes the programme.

The Harlow & Pike HVAC division had exactly these headaches. We fixed them by building a weekly numbers rhythm around live job data, tightening the pricing process, and building a management layer that meant the right decisions got made without the MD in the middle of every one.

I carry a maximum of eight clients. That's deliberate. These businesses need proper time, not a conveyor belt.

If you want to know whether the margin on your live schemes is holding, or whether you're heading for another final account that doesn't add up, take three minutes on the BOSS Scorecard at the link below. It'll show you exactly which part of the business is capping your profit right now.

Or drop me a message. No pitch, just a straight conversation.
```

_1,847 characters. Hook is in the first two lines and names the pain in Mike's own words. Short paragraphs throughout. Call to action offers both the BOSS Scorecard and a direct conversation. Add the BOSS Scorecard URL to the CTA line before publishing._

