| I've had consultants before. They wrote a report and nothing changed. | Aye, I've seen how that goes. A report describes what's wrong. It doesn't change what's happening on a live scheme next Tuesday. I don't produce a report and move on. I'm in the numbers every week. If something's slipping on a running job, I'm there to call it while there's still time to act, not six weeks later when the damage is done. That's a different thing to what you've had before. |

